    "id": "P0001",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Found **6 issues: 5 correctness defects and 1 documentation defect**. The supplied source was not edited; reproductions were added only to a scratch copy.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0002",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Async upserts can lose updates. [src/future/value_initializer.rs:350](/work/crate/src/future/value_initializer.rs:350), also line 488.  \n   Expected: same-key computations serialize their read, computation, and write. Actual: `set_waiter_value` consumes the guard before applying the operation. When insertion waits for a key lock held during an eviction listener, another upsert reads the same old value. Two increments from `1` produced `2`, rather than `3`. This loses ordinary counter or read-modify-write updates.  \n   Evidence: `future_upserts_hold_serialization_until_write` fails deterministically through public APIs.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0003",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Generation wraparound breaks LRU eviction. [src/common/concurrent/entry_info.rs:97](/work/crate/src/common/concurrent/entry_info.rs:97).  \n   Expected: policy generation follows the wrapping entry generation. Actual: `current >= value` rejects the transition from `65535` to `0`, leaving the entry marked dirty after maintenance. After 65,536 writes to one key in a capacity-one LRU cache, inserting another key retains the older key and evicts the newer one. Long-lived caches therefore stop following their configured eviction policy.  \n   Evidence: both `sync_lru_survives_generation_wrap` and `future_lru_survives_generation_wrap` fail. The synchronous control with 65,535 writes passes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0004",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Mixing fallible and infallible initialization can panic. [src/sync/value_initializer.rs:348](/work/crate/src/sync/value_initializer.rs:348), [src/future/value_initializer.rs:592](/work/crate/src/future/value_initializer.rs:592).  \n   Expected: `get_with` initializes a missing value successfully even when a concurrent fallible initializer returns an error. Actual: its waiter uses `TypeId::of::<()>`, which collides with `try_get_with` when its error type is `()`. The infallible caller receives that error and reaches `unreachable!()` at [src/sync/cache.rs:1053](/work/crate/src/sync/cache.rs:1053) or [src/future/cache.rs:1597](/work/crate/src/future/cache.rs:1597). Ordinary overlapping callers can unexpectedly panic.  \n   Evidence: synchronous and asynchronous `infallible_get_with_does_not_receive_unit_error` tests both fail.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0005",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Returning `None` from expiration update may fail to clear expiration. [src/sync/base_cache.rs:696](/work/crate/src/sync/base_cache.rs:696), [src/future/base_cache.rs:826](/work/crate/src/future/base_cache.rs:826).  \n   Expected: `expire_after_update` returning `None` clears expiration, as documented. Actual: an elapsed deadline becomes `current_duration == None`; returning `None` then skips updating the stored deadline. Replacing an expired entry before maintenance leaves the replacement expired and unavailable.  \n   Evidence: both `update_none_clears_expiration` tests create an immediately expired entry, replace it with expiration cleared, and receive `None` instead of `Some(20)`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0006",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "A weigher panic leaves synchronous initialization permanently stale. [src/sync/value_initializer.rs:153](/work/crate/src/sync/value_initializer.rs:153).  \n   Expected: after a worker panics during insertion, another caller can retry initialization of the missing key. Actual: insertion runs outside the protected initializer closure; unwinding bypasses waiter removal and leaves `Computing` stored. Subsequent initialization panics with \u201cGot unexpected state `Computing`.\u201d A single failed worker therefore prevents later initialization for that key.  \n   Evidence: `sync_get_with_recovers_after_weigher_panic` uses a weigher that panics once. After joining the failed worker, the next call still panics.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0007",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Synchronous compute documentation has broken example links. [src/sync/entry_selector.rs:201](/work/crate/src/sync/entry_selector.rs:201), also line 743.  \n   Expected: the example link opens the synchronous example. Actual: the text references `try_append_value_async.rs`, while the link definition names `try_append_value_sync.rs`. Readers get an unresolved reference.  \n   Evidence: `cargo doc` emits two `broken_intra_doc_links` warnings.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0008",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Executed checks used Rust 1.99.1 on aarch64 Linux:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0009",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Cache iterator yields expired entries that maintenance has not removed. src/common/iter.rs:117. sync::Cache iteration enumerates keys still present in the backing hash table and yields their cached values without rechecking expiration. If a value reaches its configured time-to-live while its physical entry remains pending maintenance, iter().next() can return that expired value. This affects both a newly created iterator and one created before expiration, allowing iteration-based exports to include values that should already have expired.\n\n"
  },
