    "text": "Correct the four references and document the exposed methods\u2019 execution, error, and cancellation behavior.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0098",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Eight public types lack `Debug`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0099",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Locations include `src/sync/builder.rs:50`, `src/future/builder.rs:58`, `src/common/iter.rs:22`, `src/future.rs:58`, and the four entry-selector structs.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0100",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Expected: Public helper types support diagnostic formatting.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0101",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Actual: Both builders, both iterators, and four selectors lack `Debug`, confirmed by Clippy.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0102",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Caller impact: Callers cannot directly format these objects or derive `Debug` for structures containing them.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0103",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Add manual implementations where closures or internal trait objects prevent deriving it.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0104",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Manual concurrency implementations omit their invariants\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0105",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Locations include `src/future/cache.rs:641`, `src/sync/cache.rs:576`, `src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:60`, `src/common/iter.rs:132`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0106",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Expected: Manual `Send`/`Sync` implementations explain why their bounds, ownership, and synchronization permit cross-thread use.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0107",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Actual: Thirteen implementations lack that local justification. Some comments explain why the compiler needs an implementation, without explaining the invariants that maintainers must preserve.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0108",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "invalidate_all exposes older cached values until maintenance runs. src/sync/base_cache.rs:406. In sync::Cache, invalidate_all only records valid_after and leaves the hash-table entries in place. For a previously inserted entry whose last-modified time is strictly earlier than that cutoff, a get or contains_key immediately after invalidate_all still reads the old mapping until a maintenance pass removes it. A caller that invalidates the cache after refreshing its backing data can therefore continue serving the obsolete value even though invalidation has returned.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0109",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Caller impact: Future changes to bounds or internal synchronization are harder to review correctly.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0110",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Document those invariants at each implementation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0111",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Executed checks\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0112",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Commands ran from `/work/crate`, offline, with:\n\n"
