    "report": "C",
    "text": "```sh\ncargo run --locked --manifest-path /work/tmp/probes/Cargo.toml --bin expiry\ncargo run --locked --manifest-path /work/tmp/probes/Cargo.toml --bin compute\ncargo run --locked --manifest-path /work/tmp/probes/Cargo.toml --bin timer\ncargo run --locked --manifest-path /work/tmp/probes/Cargo.toml --bin timer_async\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0124",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "All four exit 101 on the demonstrated incorrect behavior. Both timer controls pass when invoked with `-- --control`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0125",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "The `model` binary passed 10,000 mixed operations against a reference map across sync, segmented, and future caches. Scratch harness formatting and strict Clippy also passed. Logs are under `/work/tmp`, including `gate.log`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0126",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Coverage limits\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0127",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Source inspection focused on public contracts, initialization, compute serialization, expiration, maintenance, invalidation, iteration, and supporting structures. Cross-target builds, MSRV validation, Loom, trybuild-specific checks, exhaustive feature combinations, and full-crate Miri were unrun. Advisory lint candidates were not treated as independently confirmed defects.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0128",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "No dedicated security assessment, exploitability analysis, or exploit development was performed. Inquiries requiring dedicated security testing remain outside scope.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0129",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Last clock reading: **9.8997 minutes used of 15.0**."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0130",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Found **5 issues: 4 runtime correctness/error-handling issues and 1 documentation issue**. The supplied source was unchanged; targeted tests were added only to `/work/tmp/moka-review`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0131",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Async computations release serialization before applying the operation.  \n   [src/future/value_initializer.rs:350](/work/crate/src/future/value_initializer.rs:350), also line 488.  \n   The documented behavior serializes same-key compute/upsert calls. Instead, `set_waiter_value` consumes the guard and removes the waiter before the subsequent insertion or removal. Another computation can therefore read the previous value and overwrite an update.  \n   **Executed evidence:** `future_upserts_must_serialize_through_write` pauses the first insertion in its weigher and starts another increment. Both computations read `0`; the final value is `1`, expected `2`. Callers using these APIs for counters or accumulated state can lose updates. Keep serialization active through operation application.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0132",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Borrowed synchronous fallible entry lookup loses the key on a cache hit.  \n   [src/sync/cache.rs:1422](/work/crate/src/sync/cache.rs:1422).  \n   The hit path passes `false` instead of `need_key`. Consequently, `entry_by_ref(...).or_try_insert_with(...)` returns an `Entry` with no key when the value already exists. `Entry::key()` should return the cached key; it instead panics with `Bug: Key is None`.  \n   **Executed evidence:** both `sync_borrowed_try_entry_retains_key_on_hit` and `segmented_borrowed_try_entry_retains_key_on_hit` fail. The equivalent async control passes. Ordinary callers can panic while inspecting a successfully returned entry. Forward `need_key` on the hit path.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0133",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Returning `None` from an expiry update can leave the replacement expired.  \n   [src/sync/base_cache.rs:696](/work/crate/src/sync/base_cache.rs:696) and [src/future/base_cache.rs:826](/work/crate/src/future/base_cache.rs:826).  \n   An elapsed deadline becomes `current_duration = None` through `checked_duration_since`. If `expire_after_update` also returns `None`, the equality check skips clearing the existing deadline. The documented result is no expiration; the actual replacement remains immediately expired.  \n   **Executed evidence:** synchronous and async tests create an immediately expired entry, then replace it with an update callback returning `None`. Both subsequent lookups return `None`, expected `Some(2)`. Callers cannot reliably revive entries this way. Distinguish elapsed expiration from absent expiration.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0134",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "A weigher panic leaves synchronous initialization permanently stale for that key.  \n   [src/sync/value_initializer.rs:153](/work/crate/src/sync/value_initializer.rs:153).  \n   Cleanup handles a panic from `init`, but insertion and value cloning occur outside that handler. If insertion\u2019s weigher panics, the registered waiter remains `Computing` after its lock is released. Subsequent initialization attempts panic instead of retrying.  \n   **Executed evidence:** `sync_get_with_can_retry_after_weigher_panic` runs the first call in a worker thread whose weigher panics once. After joining that failed worker, a retry panics with `Got unexpected state Computing`; the equivalent async control succeeds. This is an error-recovery weakness\u2014recovery from weigher panics is not explicitly documented. Use cleanup that covers the complete waiter lifetime.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0135",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Two synchronous API example links are broken.  \n   [src/sync/entry_selector.rs:201](/work/crate/src/sync/entry_selector.rs:201) and [src/sync/entry_selector.rs:743](/work/crate/src/sync/entry_selector.rs:743).  \n   Both references name `try_append_value_async.rs`, while their link definitions name `try_append_value_sync.rs`. Readers should receive a working synchronous example link; instead, rustdoc reports unresolved links.  \n   **Executed evidence:** documentation generation with warnings denied exits `101` at these locations.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0136",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Executed project checks, from `/work/crate` with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0137",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "```sh\ncargo test --locked --features sync,future\ncargo test --locked --offline --all-features\ncargo clippy --locked --offline --features sync,future --all-targets -- -D warnings\ncargo check --locked --offline --no-default-features --features sync\ncargo check --locked --offline --no-default-features --features future\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\nRUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --locked --offline --features sync,future --no-deps\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0138",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Both test configurations passed **150 unit tests, 12 integration tests, and 67 doctests**, with five unit tests and two doctests ignored. Clippy, feature-isolated checks, and formatting passed. Strict documentation generation failed as described above.\n\n"
  },
